irl  Guide members who've told us that the  name brownies causes harm  we are sorry  Girl Guides say the change is designed  to remove one of the barriers that may  keep some girls or their families from  wanting to join the new name will be  announced in January  trouble tracking promises ahead the  report criticizing Federal efforts to  cut homelessness  [Music]  Canada's record on reducing homelessness  is in the spotlight tonight the auditor  general says the federal government  doesn't actually know whether its  efforts are curbing the crisis despite  the Liberals spending nearly 6 billion  dollars since 2018 the government can  say whether homelessness has increased  or decreased it's one of four government  performance reports released today and  there's a Common Thread Federal  organizations are often slow to use the  means at their disposal to make a  difference Eric Sorensen reports  every year in this country close to a  quarter of a million people experience  homelessness five years ago the liberal  government laid out an ambitious goal to  cut chronic homelessness in half by  2028. how's it going nobody knows says  the auditor general there isn't  sufficient data to measure outcomes you  need the information to be able to  measure where homelessness is when you  start and then whether or not you're  actually making making a difference  infrastructure Canada and Canada  mortgage and housing Corporation really  have a big data Gap we do have some data  the federal housing Minister cited tens  of thousands of people who have escaped  homelessness the last three years but he  says Community groups didn't collect as  much data as hoped because they were  coping with just getting through the  pandemic we need to do better in terms  of the collection and the analysis yes  and that part of the part of that  depends on the community entities and  they were facing the challenges of cobit  and we understand in a separate report  the auditor general says indigenous